# Used only in allowlist mode (AEGIS_FIREWALL_MODE=allowlist; the compose default is open-https, which
# ignores this file). Hosts the dev container may reach, HTTPS (443) only. firewall.sh resolves each to its IPv4 addresses
# at container start, and adds new ones every half hour; anything not listed is refused. The file is part
# of the image, so an edit takes effect at the next `make dev-up` (a rebuild), not a restart. GitHub's
# ranges come from api.github.com/meta, not this file (git, and cargo-deny's advisory database).
#
# Allowed by IP address, and CDNs share addresses between customers, so this narrows what the container
# can reach rather than sealing it. Keep the list to what dev actually needs.

